
        }
    }
}

This is a contract test for two methods in Arraylist class: Add and Remove. Test class name is ArrayListContractTest.
Test class consists of two PUT_ methods, PUT_AddContract and PUT_RemoveContract. There are four assumptions "arrList" and "x". In the PUT_AddContract method, we assume that addition of "x" to "arrList" will not affect IndexOf, LastIndexOf and Contains methods. PUT_RemoveContract method, we try removing "x" from "arrList" and all its properties should be properly evaluated after removal.
For each of the method, it assumes a precondition (i.e., everything is ok) and measures the count, indexOf, lastIndexOf, and contains of "arrList" before and after the method call. The difference between the before and after count, indexOf, lastIndexOf, and contains is evaluated for checking the functionality of the methods.

The observed (using PexObserve.ValueForViewing) values are: $old_arrList_Count, $new_arrList_Count, $old_arrList_x, $old_arrList_IndexOf_x, $new_arrList_IndexOf_x, $old_arrList_LastIndexOf_x, $new_arrList_LastIndexOf_x, $New_ret, $old_arrList_contains_x, $new_arrList_contains_x. 

