//This test class demonstrates how to use PexMethod and the other Pex class-level attributes to create parameterized unit tests for a given class.
//
//These tests are parameterized by:
//- The state of an ArrayList instance.
//- A parameter of type int that is either inserted into the list or removed from the list 
//
//To make the test more meaningful, Precondition.IsTrue is used to assume under a certain test conditions, and the method of the class is called (Add or Remove in this case). 
//
//Here, assume we use PexObserve.ValueForViewing to present the old and new values of some properties of the ArrayList instances, which can help you understand how these methods work when you call them.
//
